# Testing (TDD)

Write code TDD-style. Prefer **Feature** tests under `application/tests/Feature`.

Use **Unit** tests only for logic that runs isolated from Laravel (e.g. signature HMAC in `SignatureService`). Unit tests may extend `PHPUnit\Framework\TestCase`.

When generating tests, write **complete** coverage (happy path, validation errors, auth/policy failures, edge cases) even if some existing hand-written tests are partial.

## Conventions

- Feature tests: `RefreshDatabase`, factories, `$this->actingAs($user)` for Sanctum routes.
- Mock contracts when isolating side effects (`SignatureContract`, `AuditLogContract`).
- For audit logging assertions, use `Tests\Traits\WithAuditLogs` (`assertLog(...)`).
- Hit API routes with `/api/...` prefixes as in `routes/api.php`.
- Run tests via Docker: `docker compose exec -u www-data php php artisan test` (from `docker/`).

```php
// ✅ Feature: HTTP + DB + audit
use RefreshDatabase, WithAuditLogs;
$response = $this->actingAs($user)->post('/api/cashboxes', [...]);
$response->assertStatus(201);
$this->assertDatabaseHas('cashboxes', [...]);
$this->assertLog('cashbox-created', $user->id, cashbox_id: $cashbox->id);

// ✅ Unit: pure PHP, no Laravel TestCase
$service = new SignatureService();
$this->assertTrue($service->checkSignature($data, $key, $sig));
```
